 ### GaMeS Parametrization
-GaMeS Parametrization is a parameterization of Gaussian components into flat triangle-face meshes, allowing GS to be visualized and manipulated as a triangle soup [S3, unofficial]. For mesh-bound Gaussians, means are assigned to mesh faces via learnable barycentric coordinates of vertices, ensuring they remain bound under deformation [S3, unofficial]. The orientation of mesh-bound Gaussians is defined by the face normal and two in-plane directions derived from the vertices [S3, unofficial].
-
-**Forward Mapping:**
-Given Gaussian $N(m, R, S)$ with $R=[r_1, r_2, r_3]$ and $S=\text{diag}(\epsilon, s_2, s_3)$, the triangle vertices are:
-$$ v_1 = m, \quad v_2 = m + s_2 r_2, \quad v_3 = m + s_3 r_3 $$
-[ S3 ]
-
-**Inverse Mapping:**
-Given triangle $V=[v_1, v_2, v_3]$, the Gaussian is recovered as $N(\hat{m}, \hat{R}, \hat{S})$ using:
-$$ \hat{m} = v_1 $$
-$$ \hat{r}_1 = \frac{(v_2 - v_1) \times (v_3 - v_1)}{\|(v_2 - v_1) \times (v_3 - v_1)\|} $$
-$$ \hat{r}_2 = \frac{v_2 - v_1}{\|v_2 - v_1\|}, \quad \hat{r}_3 = \text{orth}(v_3 - v_1; \hat{r}_1, \hat{r}_2) $$
-$$ \hat{s}_1 = \epsilon, \quad \hat{s}_2 = \|v_2 - v_1\|, \quad \hat{s}_3 = \langle v_3 - v_1, \hat{r}_3 \rangle $$
-The covariance matrix is recovered as $\hat{\Sigma} = \hat{R}\hat{S}\hat{S}^T\hat{R}^T$ [ S3 ].
